From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:34:49 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 48/66] hostapd: keep the channel of a forced ubus channel
 switch on an ACS radio

switch_chan with force falls back to restarting the interface on the
new channel when the CSA fails (e.g. a DFS target). On a radio with an
automatic channel, that restart cleared the channel again and ran ACS,
so the radio came up wherever ACS chose, not where it was sent (B52).
hostapd's own CHAN_SWITCH marks the restart with is_ch_switch_dfs, which
keeps the channel through that one setup; do the same in the ubus
fallback.

Bump PKG_RELEASE.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
---
 package/network/services/hostapd/Makefile          | 2 +-
 package/network/services/hostapd/src/src/ap/ubus.c | 3 +++
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/package/network/services/hostapd/Makefile b/package/network/services/hostapd/Makefile
index 532fd5239b..de7d4ce1ac 100644
--- a/package/network/services/hostapd/Makefile
+++ b/package/network/services/hostapd/Makefile
@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@
 include $(TOPDIR)/rules.mk
 
 PKG_NAME:=hostapd
-PKG_RELEASE:=6
+PKG_RELEASE:=7
 
 PKG_SOURCE_URL:=https://w1.fi/hostap.git
 PKG_SOURCE_PROTO:=git
diff --git a/package/network/services/hostapd/src/src/ap/ubus.c b/package/network/services/hostapd/src/src/ap/ubus.c
index c33f57ca7c..0fc1c6d8e7 100644
--- a/package/network/services/hostapd/src/src/ap/ubus.c
+++ b/package/network/services/hostapd/src/src/ap/ubus.c
@@ -1125,6 +1125,9 @@ static void switch_chan_fallback_cb(void *eloop_data, void *user_ctx)
 	struct hostapd_iface *iface = eloop_data;
 	struct hostapd_freq_params *freq_params = user_ctx;
 
+	/* keep the new channel through the restart, as CHAN_SWITCH does; on
+	 * an ACS radio the setup would otherwise clear it and run ACS */
+	iface->is_ch_switch_dfs = true;
 	hostapd_switch_channel_fallback(iface, freq_params);
 }
 
